1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,541
Second, quickly, the nucleophile attacks.

2
00:00:03,541 --> 00:00:14,752
Because the carbocation is flat, it can attack from either face with equal ease, so a single enantiomer gives a fifty fifty mixture of both products: racemisation.

3
00:00:14,752 --> 00:00:21,171
And since hydroxide only arrives after the slow step, it does not appear in the rate law at all.

4
00:00:21,171 --> 00:00:25,755
Rate equals k times the haloalkane concentration only.

